Let $\Omega\subset\mathbb{R}^n$ be a bounded domain and suppose $f\in L^2(\Omega)$ is given. A function\[u\in H^{2k}(\Omega)\cap H_0^k(\Omega)\]is a \textbf{strong solution} of the Dirichlet problem if
\begin{equation}\label{eq:strong-dirichlet-divergence-equation}
L(\bm{x},D)u=\sum_{0\leq|\sigma|,|\gamma|\leq k}(-1)^{|\sigma|}D^\sigma(a_{\sigma\gamma}(\bm{x})D^\gamma u)=f
\end{equation}
in $\Omega$.

